- op: discuss  # 5f5a
  at: '2026-06-07T06:38:19Z'  # 5f5a
  by: agent  # 5f5a
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 5f5a
  clock: 2  # 5f5a
  nonce: 5f5a  # 5f5a
  message: "Dogfood finding (members F145.A2-a, F152.A2, F153.A2 — cluster C1), reproduces on the frozen substrate. Mechanism: when a dataclass field is an open Dict[str,Any] or a type the dataclass->schema generator cannot introspect, it falls back to a bare {\"type\":\"object\"} with no properties (and no additionalProperties typing). Scope: at least 5 schema sites emit contentless objects — the top-level limits $def, plus Edge.quality, Symbol.quality, Symbol.meta, and UsageContext.metadata — each declared as an object whose internal structure the schema does not describe. Affects every behavior-map consumer that reads the published schema as the contract for these payloads. Exposure/consequence: consumers must reverse-engineer these payloads from sample output rather than from the contract; an agent generating code against the schema will not know meta can carry evidence/channel/protocol keys, that quality can carry score/reason, etc. Expectation: schema definitions describe the keys a consumer can rely on (properties, or at least additionalProperties typing), so the published schema documents the payload rather than asserting \"some object.\" This is the generator-level root cause; consumers downstream include U08 (limits sub-fields undocumented, WI-zugof) and the Node.meta/Edge.meta key-vocabulary rows. Cross-ref WI-zugof (limits sub-fields), WI-mirig (Node.meta undocumented sub-keys), WI-vusot (axis_meta_keys registry)."  # 5f5a
- op: discuss  # abc7
  at: '2026-06-08T03:21:53Z'  # abc7
  by: agent  # abc7
