  message: "Re-surfaced in dogfooding tranche 10 (U08, F191.A1 split, severity 3). 'limits' is {type:object} with zero sub-properties in schema.json — the entire block is schema-opaque, the case this item names as the dataclass->schema generator emitting contentless {type:object} for un-introspected fields. Fix: add a Limits $defs/sub-property schema."  # abc7
- op: discuss  # dcb3
  at: '2026-06-11T17:21:40Z'  # dcb3
  by: agent  # dcb3
  actor: jgstern_agent  # dcb3
  clock: 4  # dcb3
  nonce: dcb3  # dcb3
  message: "[Wave-0 hygiene re-verify] **PARTIALLY FIXED:**\n\nSchema half: Limits (the $def) is **RESOLVED**. The Limits class now has proper typed nested structures via FailedFile, ClassificationFailure, AmbiguousPath, SupplyChainLimits specs (scripts/generate_schema_lib.py:715-854). Edge.meta composite is properly documented (lines 501-549).\n\n**REMAINS:**\n- Symbol.quality: `Optional[Dict[str,Any]]` → contentless in schema (scripts/generate_schema_lib.py:434)\n- Symbol.meta: `Optional[Dict[str,Any]]` → contentless in schema (line 435)\n- Edge.quality: `Optional[Dict[str,Any]]` → contentless in schema (line 645)\n- Feature.node_depths/node_tiers/admission_stats: `Dict[str,int]` → contentless objects without additionalProperties (scripts/generate_schema_lib.py:939-943)\n\nPer spec.md §8, Edge.meta carries evidence_type/evidence_lang/evidence_spans (already handled as composite). Symbol.quality and Edge.quality are described in spec as {score, reason}. Feature dictionary fields need typed additionalProperties declarations.\n\nNOTE: Tracker item mentions UsageContext.metadata and Pattern fields — these classes are not in generate_schema_lib specs; they don't serialize to behavior map schema. This scope may be stale."  # dcb3
- op: discuss  # fcd3
  at: '2026-07-30T17:20:27Z'  # fcd3
  by: agent  # fcd3
  actor: jgstern_agent  # fcd3
  clock: 5  # fcd3
  nonce: fcd3  # fcd3
  message: "ADVANCED (not closed) by this session's schema work, and re-measured so the residual is exact.\n\nThe item names five contentless {\"type\": \"object\"} emissions: limits, Edge.quality, Symbol.quality, Symbol.meta, UsageContext.metadata. Two are already gone for other reasons — Edge.quality was REMOVED entirely at SCHEMA_VERSION 0.20.0 (D9b R4, register pt.30), and Symbol.meta now carries 47 registry-derived properties after the WI-zisig fix in this session (Edge.meta likewise went 2 -> 34).\n\nMeasured remainder: 10 contentless object schemas, of which UsageContext.metadata is the only one this item names by name. The other 9 are metrics.languages / metrics.by_supply_chain_tier (additionalProperties), the *.items of AnalysisRun.skipped_passes / AnalysisRun.failed_files / Limits.skipped_passes / Limits.truncated_files, and Feature.node_depths / node_tiers / admission_stats.\n\nWorth noting for whoever takes it: the WI-zisig fix is a reusable shape only where a REGISTRY already enumerates the keys. These 10 have no such registry, so they need either a dataclass to introspect or hand-authored properties — which is the same judgement WI-libib's author made when rejecting the full 312-cell matrix as over-broad. Not a mechanical repeat of what just landed."  # fcd3
